# Moved 0.1.10 -> 0.1.11 in #2569, closing a memory-corruption bug rather
# than unblocking a build. The pinned 0.1.10 oracle emits a 64-bit atomic
# access through a 32-bit pointer at 38 sites in runtime/** (34 stores + 4
# CAS, identical count on aarch64-macos, aarch64-linux and x86_64-linux):
# `atomicStore`/`atomicCmpxchg` against `spinUnlocked`/`spinLocked: i32`
# lock cells (runtime/spinlock.bit:46-47) emitted the `x`-register (64-bit)
# form of `stlr`/`ldaxr`/`stlxr` instead of the `w`-register (32-bit) form
# the `*i32` pointee requires under `atomicStore(p: *T, v: T)`
# (spec/SPEC.md:853, §11.5) — a 4-byte out-of-bounds write past every lock
# cell it touches. `6a8977a3` ("Fix #2429: untyped int/rune constants into
# f32/f64 stored the integer bit pattern") fixed this as an invisible side
# effect, by adding the const's own declared-type hint at
# compiler/lowerdriver.bit:437-451 — a float-literal ticket, not an atomics
# ticket. That commit post-dates v0.1.10 (`git merge-base --is-ancestor
# 6a8977a3 v0.1.10` is false; true for v0.1.11), so no existing release
# could have closed this — same shape as the 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10 entry above,
# which says the same thing about its own missing symbol.
#
# THE SHAPE OF THIS MOVE DIFFERS FROM 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10. There, the old
# stage0 could not build `tools/build` AT ALL — a missing runtime symbol,
# an outright E0078 on every fresh clone. Here, the old stage0 builds the
# tree FINE; it is simply WRONG about atomic access width, and got away
# with it by luck of layout: every lock cell in this tree today sits
# 8-byte aligned inside a 16-byte-slotted module cell or a whole `i64`
# struct-field slot, so the extra 4 bytes landed in padding rather than a
# neighbour. This repin bakes in a correctness fix that a working build
# could not have surfaced on its own — full disassembly, the ruled-out
# dangerous direction (a narrow const writing into a WIDE cell, checked
# across the entire tree and found not to occur), and the `maps.bit`
# `u64` tag (a second, behaviorally-inert divergence from the same
# commit) are recorded on #2569's own comments. The shipped-release
# exposure of the 64-bit form in 0.1.10 is #2742 (p0, filed separately,
# not a repin matter).
